  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>DNP</mi></math> test is useful for the identification of carbonyl compounds.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">The 2,4-dinitrophenylhydrazine can be used as a process for the identification of aldehydes and ketones.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">The formed 2,4-dinitrophenylhydrazone is a solid that is purified and the melting point is determined. The comparison of a melting point with a table of known values could identify the compound as aldehyde or ketone</p>",
